# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable bulk. Everything here is reproducible from the scripts; the
# expensive-to-recompute RESULTS (per-replicate JSON, aggregated CSVs) are
# tracked. See README section 20 for which script regenerates what.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Rosetta structure ensembles (~1.7 GB) -- regenerate with 06/21/25/31
results/*/pdb/

# MD trajectories, restarts, topologies and per-stage outputs (~6 GB)
# regenerate with 38_md_prep.py -> 38b_md_build.py -> 39_md_run.sh
data/md/*/rep*/*.nc
data/md/*/rep*/*.rst7
data/md/*/rep*/*.out
data/md/*/rep*/*.info
data/md/*/rep*/*.in
data/md/*/system.prmtop
data/md/*/system.inpcrd
data/md/*/system_solvated.pdb
data/md/*/bench/

# Downloaded homolog structures (~204 MB) -- refetch with 08_homolog_cavities.py --stage fetch
results/homolog_cavities/raw/
results/homolog_cavities/domains/
results/homolog_cavities/ca_traces/
results/homolog_cavities/subdb_exp*
results/foldseek/

# Verbose job logs; the curated analysis logs (logs/*.txt) ARE tracked
logs/*.log
logs/units*/

# Third-party supplementary data is deliberately NOT vendored here.
# Tian et al. xlsx files live outside the repo at
#   /bigdata/cutlerlab/jjaco081/mutation_prediction_benchmark/
# Redistributing publisher supplementary files may breach their terms.
*.xlsx

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# downloaded PDB structures for the floppy-ligand survey (regenerable)
data/survey_cache/

# regenerable viewing trajectories (rebuild with scripts/41_md_view.sh)
data/md/view/

# LigandMPNN per-sequence structure dumps (~156 MB) -- regenerate with
# 48b_submit_stage1_lmpnn.sh. The scientifically load-bearing outputs, the
# sampling_probs in stats/*.pt and the sequences in seqs/*.fa, ARE tracked.
results/stage1*/*/backbones/

# the apo-bug run, kept on disk as evidence but too bulky to version (166 MB);
# README section 23h records what it was and why it is retracted
results/stage1_RETRACTED_apo_bug/

# Rosetta stage-1 scratch: timing probes and the per-task input copies
results/stage1_rosetta_smoke/
results/stage1_rosetta/_input_*.pdb
results/stage1_rosetta/_k59_input.pdb
results/stage1_rosetta_fnsweep/*/_input_*.pdb
results/stage1_rosetta_fnsweep/*/pdb/

# Loop-dynamics per-frame time series (~95 MB of cpptraj .dat, one row per frame)
# regenerate with 58_loop_dynamics_prep.py -> 58b_loop_dynamics_run.sh (minutes).
# The VERIFIED RESIDUE MAP and the aggregated summary are tracked -- the map is a
# correctness artefact, not bulk data.
data/loop_dynamics/*/rep*/*.dat
data/loop_dynamics/*/rep*/*.in
data/loop_dynamics/*/rep*/*.log

# Second-generation MD systems (191-aa rebuild, README 28). Same rule as data/md/:
